Daniel Kraft wrote:
> Hi,
> 
> I've just started to play, and just came across some problem in Sokoban: 
> Multiple times, there were monsters behind the boulders so I wasn't able 
> to move them when I had no chance to come behind the boulder another way.
> 
> I first tried throwing objects at it to have it killed, but most of the 
> time this did not do it; so the only other possibility I saw was to drop 
> all my stuff and get behind the boulder--this way I was able to 
> fight/kill it, but only without armor and weapons; finally, this ended 
> fatally...
> 
> Is there some clever trick I can do when I come into such situations the 
> next time?

No clever trick, but straightforward, I'd say, given that you already know
what to do. :-)

Get more projectiles to throw; get stones from the main dungeon if you
have nothing else. Or unstrip as you've done, but try to keep a weapon;
that's possible if you are not too week. And retreat to heal if you're
low on HPs! (Leave the level while healing so that the monster's healing
counter won't progress.) It's also possible to zap some types of wands,
like magic missile, fire, cold, lightning, which won't affect boulders.
You can also squeeze onto the boulder square and teleport the beast away.

